    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Space Raiders** (1983) represents Roger Corman's attempt to capitalize on the space opera craze following **Star Wars** (1977), recycling space footage from his earlier film **Battle Beyond the Stars** (1980). The film follows a familiar pattern of space pirates with hearts of gold, but stands out for putting a 10-year-old boy at the center of its story. While clearly made on a shoestring budget, it captures that distinctly 1980s direct-to-video sci-fi charm that influenced films like **The Last Starfighter** (1984) and **Enemy Mine** (1985)."
      },
